model g6_refusal_keys
  tally 2
  on 2025-12-31
  start 2025-01-01
  end 2025-12-31
  note "T, issue #55, G6: which refusal a place keeps (E §4.1, E §4.2 step 4; tally 2.1.2's text order, #57 asks the spec): one plan move m of two keys, a place and a flat of a list index, with two instances on one day, m[x, f3] and m[y, f11], each a leg into gone after its lifespan ends (RUN-LIFESPAN), both refused at src. The legs are booked in their order's text, keys quoted, where m[x, f3]'s sorts first, so bal(src) prints m[x, f3].cash. Its twin's m[x, f3] is a leg of 0, so m[y, f11].cash refuses alone."

source fixture "T's fixture for S's kernel tests (invented values)"

unit DUK: currency minor 0.01

index flats = [f1, f2, f3, f4, f5, f6, f7, f8, f9, f10, f11]

input amt: money DUK

input d0: date

place src: accounts DUK lives 2025-01-01..

place gone: accounts DUK lives 2025-01-01..2025-01-05

place x: accounts DUK lives 2025-01-01..

place y: accounts DUK lives 2025-01-01..

move m[p in accounts on d0, f in flats]: transfers
  on d0
  when (p == x and pos(f) == 3) or (p == y and pos(f) == 11)
  leg cash from src to gone amount amt

ask q: bal(src, 2025-01-31)

version facts
  cite fixture
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  amt = 1.00 DUK
  d0 = 2025-01-10
  opening[src] = 500.00 DUK at 2025-01-01 start
  opening[gone] = 0 DUK at 2025-01-01 start
  opening[x] = 0 DUK at 2025-01-01 start
  opening[y] = 0 DUK at 2025-01-01 start
